{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-ext-deriv","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Example","doco:Section"],"label":"ex:q-ext-deriv","kind":"example","title":"$q$-Deformed exterior derivative","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-reeb-decomposition","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-categorical-dq-squared"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-ext-deriv","tags":["exterior-derivative","archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.qExtDeriv","text":"q-ext-deriv.md","leanSource":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-ext-deriv.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"ex:q-ext-deriv\"></a><p>In the archimedean realisation, the categorical <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q</code> specialises to <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q \\colon \\Omega^k(M) \\to \\Omega^{k+1}(M)</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  d_q\\alpha = q^{-1}d\\alpha + (1 - q^{-1})\\varTheta \\wedge \\mathcal{L}_\\xi\\alpha.</code></pre>\n<p>The vertical projection <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\pi_V \\circ d</code> becomes <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varTheta \\wedge \\mathcal{L}_\\xi</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2 = q^{-1}(1-q^{-1})d\\varTheta \\wedge \\mathcal{L}_\\xi</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-ext-deriv.md","heading":"Example","number":"3.19.1"}
